From 283602e35a4f308a5bb6e1ed39038928768d3723 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: evilcomputer12 <martinrobotika@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:49:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] xgameruntime: Complete every XStore async request
 instead of leaving it pending

The store back end (catalog, purchases, package updates, license tokens,
collections/purchase ids, store UI) is not implemented. Those *Async methods
returned E_NOTIMPL without touching the XAsyncBlock, so a title waiting on
the block with XAsyncGetStatus(wait=TRUE) or on its completion callback
would hang. They now validate their arguments (E_GAMERUNTIME_INVALID_HANDLE
for a missing context/query handle, E_POINTER for a missing async block)
and complete from a worker thread with E_GAMESTORE_NETWORK_ERROR; the
matching Result/ResultSize/ResultCount calls return that HRESULT through
XAsyncGetResult/XAsyncGetResultSize with their out parameters zeroed.

Two queries succeed with an empty answer instead, because that is the true
state of an installed Game Pass base game and titles call them routinely:
XStoreQueryAddOnLicenses (count 0) and XStoreQueryEntitledProducts (an
empty product query handle that XStoreEnumerateProductsQuery accepts,
XStoreProductsQueryHasMorePages answers FALSE for and
XStoreCloseProductsQueryHandle frees).

Also move the force-close watchdog call in InitializeApiImplEx2 after the
declarations (-Wdeclaration-after-statement).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
